      {
        "id": 1858183624,
        "content": "We only have inheritance on top level properties, so if `incentives` property is missing from repo and org config, it will use the whole `incentives` property from default config. Nested properties don't have inheritance (if `h1` is not present in repo config it won't inherit from default config), that is something I was meaning to make an issue for.\r\n_Originally posted by @whilefoo in https://github.com/ubiquity/ubiquibot/pull/545#discussion_r1297266427_\r\nFor example if we have a organization config:\r\n```yaml\r\nincentives:\r\n  comment:\r\n    elements:\r\n      code: 5\r\n      img: 5\r\n      h1: 1\r\n    totals:\r\n      word: 0.1\r\n```\r\nand repo config:\r\n```yaml\r\nincentives:\r\n  comment:\r\n    elements:\r\n      code: 10\r\n      li: 3\r\n    totals:\r\n      word: 0.1\r\n```\r\ncurrently because repo config overrides organization config and we parse only top-level properties, the merged config will be the same as repo config, but we want to have inheritance on nested properties too, so the merge config should look like this:\r\n```yaml\r\nincentives:\r\n  comment:\r\n    elements:\r\n      code: 10\r\n      img: 5\r\n      li: 3\r\n      h1: 1\r\n    totals:\r\n      word: 0.1\r\n```",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity/ubiquibot/issues/648",
        "commentType": "ISSUE_SPECIFICATION",
        "score": {
          "reward": 4.31,
          "formatting": {
            "content": {
              "p": {
                "score": 0,
                "elementCount": 5
              },
              "em": {
